 December each came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 5 grids. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, April to May ran 176% of normal and November to December just 40%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 27% on the middle of the grids. Grid 19662 shows a preliminary August to September 2026 estimate of 38.8, and every grid had its driest year in 1963.</p>"}
